{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-34291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-34291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]=5[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=5{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}-5{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 5{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-34291" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3feb68d2b84414e17c2b4f276fc60294c1532450420fca1c0db8e320007d057"} {"question" "q-34291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-34291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-34291" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-75645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-75645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is\n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=-2[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=-2{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}-2{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-75645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3feb68d2b84414e17c2b4f276fc60294c1532450420fca1c0db8e320007d057"} {"question" "q-75645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-75645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-75645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-105296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-105296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}-\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-105296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3feb68d2b84414e17c2b4f276fc60294c1532450420fca1c0db8e320007d057"} {"question" "q-105296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-105296" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned