=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-75640" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3feb68d2b84414e17c2b4f276fc60294c1532450420fca1c0db8e320007d057"} {"question" "q-75640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-75640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-75640" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-34142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-34142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]=-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]=-3{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}-3{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 3{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-34142" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3feb68d2b84414e17c2b4f276fc60294c1532450420fca1c0db8e320007d057"} {"question" "q-34142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-34142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-34142" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $-{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2} & =-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3feb68d2b84414e17c2b4f276fc60294c1532450420fca1c0db8e320007d057"} {"question" "q-157253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $-6{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-{a}_{3} & =-6[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12-8-4 \\\\ -6+4+2 \\\\ -12+7+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}=6,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3feb68d2b84414e17c2b4f276fc60294c1532450420fca1c0db8e320007d057"} {"question" "q-157252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $-{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+5{a}_{3}=0.$\n- ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly dependent." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}+5{a}_{3} & =-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2+0+15 \\\\ -7-10+20 \\\\ 0+0+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we can reorder the equations in this system as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is true, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/state.json" "file_sha256" "eab163623da2ffe881c32948886fa8fb98a0929bc61bb83c10ac41813cb265d4"} {"question" "q-157228" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044078/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3feb68d2b84414e17c2b4f276fc60294c1532450420fca1c0db8e320007d057"} {"que